+| Candidate | Mechanism, prerequisites, limitations, burden and eligibility | Decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| Retain current | No changes/dependencies; recovery through search/API possible, but identical option labels persist | Rejected for accepted F01 |
+| Internal contextual labels | Existing Rust/native HTML and report metadata; no services, accounts, credentials or new licenses/tools. Existing hardware; tiny per-request map, longer labels on 81 nodes. Fully tested through app and standalone public renderer | D01 selected; eligibility no addition required, manifests/lock unchanged |
+| Internal Rust/WASM autocomplete | No new execution dependency inherently required; would need new widget/state/keyboard handling and assistive-technology validation. Reduced scrolling is an unmeasured hypothesis; native-HTML fallback must remain. W3C code not copied or integrated | Not added. Reconsider with measured discovery barrier and successful host/assistive-technology prototype |
+| Hosted identity/retrieval integration | No concrete candidate has a verified free/accountless/credentialless path or measured benefit for this UI gap; transitive prerequisites and eligibility remain unknown | Unestablished and kept out; no service execution added |
+
+Existing Rust/Cargo, Python, Node/Playwright/Chromium and Jev dependencies remain baseline constraints. No runtime, build, dev, test backend or transitive package was added. The research/judgment tools were used through existing configured access; they were not made project dependencies. E08 verifies deterministic runtime with empty HOME and no inherited credentials, using existing compiled artifacts and committed reports; it does not claim a clean-machine Rust installation. No software/service purchase or new signup occurred.
+
+## Jev and review boundaries
+
+See [judgment resolutions](evidence/judgment-resolutions.md) for all consequential uncertainty, raw-distribution links, negative controls, classification rules, and the initial patch escalation. Jev's contradictory/unstable aspect judgments and erroneous hypothetical dependency check are preserved. The initial review's `safe_to_apply=.79`, test-gap confidence `.31`, and blast-radius confidence `.37` were reported to the user; stronger host source review plus equal-era/metadata-free/browser/full-network checks address the specific uncertainty. No threshold lowered or unchanged decision repeatedly sampled for approval.
+
+Loaded skill hashes: adversarial-ux-test v2.0.0 `c790dcbd617e5481e50fd5aeb432526ef976c14db011b2631ea3f4f73697f157`; Jev `0a5acb5d5e2c4681e8fcf908fece465ef47c703feee0d3827e101c3aaee8fa40`. Saved judgments use `typesafe/jev-1.13-20260917` via configured OpenRouter. No inference-provider output is independent historical corroboration. `jgrep` exit codes were checked (matches 0, no clean error); original path-location and diff-self-check results retained. No applicable new executable third-party research artifact was run.
